title: Balance simulations
intro: Each class against each enemy, thousands of times, by the game's own rules.
project: Empty | Balance
write: Tables/Classes.table | balance-simulations/Classes.table
write: Tables/Enemies.table | balance-simulations/Enemies.table
write: Scenes/Arena.scene | balance-simulations/Arena.scene
scene: Arena

chapter: An arena and two tables | Data > New Simulation
explain: entity:Hero | The arena | The arena is a scene of the game: a hero and an enemy taking turns, each chasing the other and hitting what it walks into, each taking its health and damage from a row of a table.
say: The Classes table gives a warrior, a mage and a rogue health and damage that grow with their level, and the Enemies table a slime, a goblin and an ogre, with the gold and XP they're worth.
say: Data, New Simulation sets up a matchup from the open scene: its entities with Table Values are the two sides.
menu: Data > New Simulation...
prompt: Balance
expectsim: arena = Arena
expectsim: first:entity = Hero
expectsim: first:table = Classes
expectsim: second:table = Enemies
explain: sims:settings | The settings | Each class plays each enemy, the number of runs each, with random numbers from a seed. Every change is saved to the simulation's file, and Control Z undoes it.
simset: runs = 300
expectsim: runs = 300
spot: sims:size | Nine pairs, three hundred runs each

chapter: Thousands of fights | Run
say: Run plays them all headless, as fast as the computer goes, on every core. The same seed plays the same fights on any machine.
simrun
explain: sims:summary | What came of it | Two thousand seven hundred fights in a second or so, and how often the classes won.
expectfinding: Ogre is beaten in 0%
explain: sims:findings | What stands out | Pairs where one side always wins, and a row far from the rest: nobody beats the ogre at level one.
explain: sims:results | Every pair | Each pair's win rate, turns, damage dealt and taken, and the gold and XP it earned.
simtab: Matrix
expectmatrix: Warrior > Slime = 100%
expectmatrix: Mage > Ogre = 0%
explain: sims:matrix | The matrix | Every pair, coloured by how one-sided it is: orange where the class wins, blue where the enemy does, plain where it's even.
spot: sims:chart | Each class's win rate over all the enemies

chapter: Each class at each level | A sweep
say: A sweep plays the whole matchup again with a column changed by steps. Here, each class's level, from one to eight, against the ogre.
simset: second:rows = Ogre
simset: sweeps = true
expectsim: sweep:table = Classes
expectsim: sweep:column = Level
simset: sweep:to = 8
expectsim: sweep:to = 8
simrun
simtab: Sweep
explain: sims:chart | Win rate over the levels | A line for each class: where it starts beating the ogre, levels that change nothing, and levels that jump, which the findings name.
expectfinding: Level

chapter: A fight, turn by turn | Over a Run
simtab: Over a Run
simset: step = Level 6
simset: pair = Warrior vs Ogre
explain: sims:chart | Health over a fight | Each side's health as the fight goes, a point a turn, averaged over the runs.

chapter: Anything else in a script | SimulationScript
say: Anything else is a short script. This gauntlet sends each hero through every enemy in turn, with the arena's own fights, adding up the gold and XP as it goes.
write: Scripts/Gauntlet.cs | balance-simulations/Gauntlet.cs
code: Assets/Scripts/Gauntlet.cs | Gauntlet.cs
hidecode
simset: sweeps = false
simset: second:table =
simset: second:rows =
simset: script = Gauntlet
expectsim: script = Gauntlet
simrun
simtab: Over a Run
simset: pair = Warrior vs Enemy
explain: sims:chart | Gold and XP over a run | What a warrior earns as it fights its way through, until the ogre stops it.
say: Agents run simulations too, and read every result, through the editor's MCP.
